---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Dark Energy Theory Cheat Sheet | Free Cosmological Constant, Quintessence, Phantom"
  description="Complete dark energy theory cheat sheet with cosmological constant, quintessence, and phantom energy. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Energy Theory<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Cosmological constant, quintessence, and phantom energy. From Einstein to modern cosmology.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cosmological Constant</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>w = -1 (exactly)
ρ_Λ = constant (doesn't dilute)
Einstein's "biggest blunder"
Problem: ρ_obs vs ρ_predicted differs by 10¹²⁰</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Quintessence</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Dynamic scalar field
w varies with time
Not constant like Λ
Can evolve: w(t) = w₀ + wₐ(1-a)
Requires new physics beyond ΛCDM</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Phantom Energy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>w < -1
Energy density increases with time
Violates null energy condition
Big Rip scenario
Most observations consistent with w ≈ -1</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Modified Gravity</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Alternatives</h3>
        <pre><code>f(R) gravity: modify Einstein-Hilbert action
DGP braneworld: extra dimensions
MOND: modify Newton's second law
Emergent gravity: entropic forces
Status: all face observational constraints</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Observational Constraints</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Current Limits</h3>
        <pre><code>w = -1.03 ± 0.03 (Planck + SNe)
Ω_Λ = 0.685 ± 0.007 (Planck 2018)
Consistent with cosmological constant
No evidence for dynamics yet</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
